  gcc-14/clang-19 -no-pie subject.s -o program
  ./program
All ten native mode/assembler combinations exit 0; both assembler combinations
for iso-c99-language-mode.c also exit 0. The focused test separately checks
normal undeclared-call rejection, bare GNU keyword rejection in ISO mode,
reserved keyword spellings, final-option reduction and user macro overrides.
No original application pass is inferred from these tailored checks.
